<%- include('partials/header') %>
  <style>
    .faq-container {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 4rem auto;
      padding: 2rem;
    }

    .faq-item {
      background: var(--card-bg);
      border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      border-radius: 12px;
    }

    .faq-question {
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      color: #fff;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .faq-answer {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .faq-highlight {
      color: var(--accent-gold);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
  </style>

  <div class="faq-container">
    <h1 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: white;">Organizer FAQ</h1>
    <p style="text-align: center; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      Empowering competition organizers with unparalleled digital reach and brand visibility.
    </p>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">What is AwardHome?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        AwardHome hosts <span class="faq-highlight">curated digital trophy cases</span> for
        competitive-dance families: results from competitions across the country live on as the permanent
        <span class="faq-highlight">portfolios of thousands of dancers and studios</span>. Every award
        becomes a shareable award card that dancers post on social media, use for college recruiting, and
        embed on studio websites — and every card from your events carries your competition's name and
        brand. Instead of results that get lost over time — expired links, retired portals, forgotten
        PDFs — your awards keep working for you year after year: at minimum a free backup of your award
        data, at best
        <span class="faq-highlight">ongoing brand visibility</span> everywhere your dancers share their wins.
        And we point that attention back to you: organizers are encouraged to
        <span class="faq-highlight">link their own websites and registration pages</span> and to show their
        future tour dates in our <a href="/dance/events" style="color: var(--accent-gold);">Upcoming Events
        directory</a> — right where studios and families plan next season.
        <br><br>
        See for yourself. Here's a card for a fictional competition, exactly as a
        dancer would share it. Flip it over and page to the end: the closing
        <span class="faq-highlight">&ldquo;Presented by&rdquo;</span> page carries the
        organizer's mark — that one is yours.
        <%- include('partials/demo_card', { demo: { colophonMessage: 'Where every feather is earned on stage.' } }) %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">Some of our events or seasons are missing — how do we add them?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        If you've claimed your organizer account, head to the <span class="faq-highlight">Upload Results</span>
        tab on your dashboard — add a single event, or send several seasons at once as one zip (or email us a
        Google Drive / Dropbox link if that's easier). If you haven't claimed your account yet, just email
        <span class="faq-highlight">hello@awardhome.com</span> naming the missing events, ideally with the
        results attached or linked, and we'll take care of the rest. Either way, the new events join your
        existing archive, and our team sees that every award lands in the right dancer and studio portfolios.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">My competition isn't on AwardHome yet — how do we join?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        We'd love to have you — just email <span class="faq-highlight">hello@awardhome.com</span> from your
        organization and tell us about your competition. If you have results handy in any format — CSV, Excel,
        PDFs, database exports, one event or your entire history as a zip or a Google Drive / Dropbox link —
        include them and we'll usually have a live page for your competition within a few days. If not, no
        problem: reach out first and we'll figure out the easiest path together.
        <br><br>
        There's <span class="faq-highlight">zero technical work on your end</span> — our team
        handles all the processing — free for organizers. Once your page is live, we'll send you a
        private access link to claim your organizer dashboard, where you can upload future results, set up your
        marketing profile, and get your logo onto every award card from your events.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">Can we do custom branding of the award cards?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        Yes — when you claim your Organizer profile, you gain access to a powerful set of branding tools. First, you can set
        a custom <span class="faq-highlight">Slogan and Event Description</span> to market your competition directly
        on your public page on our site.
        <br><br>
        Second, you can upload your official logo. Using our interactive display sliders, you can set the size and
        transparency of your logo — then our design team hand-fits it onto the "Trophy Cards" displayed on dancer
        portfolios before it goes live, so every card your dancers share looks polished, usually within a day or two.
        <br><br>
        Finally, you can upload specific <span class="faq-highlight">Custom Trophy Icons</span> mapped precisely to
        your award taxonomy. Want a Crown icon for Title Winners and a Diamond for Platinum adjudication? You can
        configure it all, completely replacing our default icons and turning every award won at your event into an
        enduring personalized advertisement for your competition.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">How do we claim our organizer account?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        Organizer accounts are activated by invitation to keep every competition's page in the right hands. Email
        <span class="faq-highlight">hello@awardhome.com</span> from an official address for your organization
        (or from the contact listed on your competition's website), and once we've verified it's really you,
        we'll send a <span class="faq-highlight">private access link</span> that connects your account to your
        organization — the whole process usually takes a day or two, and setup itself takes about two minutes.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">What does this cost?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        Hosting your results, the concierge data processing, the organizer dashboard, branding on award
        cards — <span class="faq-highlight">most features are free for organizers</span>, and with our
        sponsors' help we aim to keep them free for as long as we can. Real people and real servers do
        the work behind the platform, so if AwardHome brings your organization value, sponsoring is the
        best way to help — we'd love to hear from you at
        <span class="faq-highlight">hello@awardhome.com</span> or through the
        <a href="/partners" style="color: var(--accent-gold);">partners page</a>.
        <br><br>
        The first way to sponsor is <span class="faq-highlight">optional gold
          registration-button highlighting</span>: in the <a href="/dance/events"
          style="color: var(--accent-gold);">Upcoming Events
          directory</a>, where studios plan their season, featured events
        carry a <span class="faq-highlight">gold Register button</span> instead of the standard one. Every
        organizer's <span class="faq-highlight">first gold button is free</span> — place it on any event from
        your dashboard's Upcoming Events tab. Each gold button stays with its event through show day;
        once that event has taken place, your free button is yours to place on the next one. Additional
        gold buttons are available per event starting <span class="faq-highlight">October 15, 2026</span>
        (if some of your events have not filled up by then and need a gentle push) — each costs about
        <span class="faq-highlight">one solo registration fee at your own event</span>; email
        <span class="faq-highlight">hello@awardhome.com</span>. Please note listing
        order, dates, and results are not sponsored.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">What is the "Presented by" page on award cards?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        Award cards can flip into a mini-book, and the closing page is your colophon: your approved logo shown
        large, your organization's name, and an optional one-line tagline (set it on your Branding page under
        "Card 'Presented by' Tagline"). It appears on every card from your events once our design team has fitted
        and approved your logo — your brand on every card dancers share, including the flip side.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">I saw the Upcoming Events directory — some of our tour dates are missing. Can we add them?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        Yes — open the <span class="faq-highlight">Upcoming Events</span> tab on your dashboard and add each stop —
        city, dates, venue, and your registration link. Listings appear on your public page and in the
        <a href="/dance/events" style="color: var(--accent-gold);">Upcoming Events directory</a>, where studios and
        parents browse
        when planning next season's competitions — sorted by distance from them, with your events one star-tap
        from their shortlist and one click from their family calendar. Every complete listing is a registration
        channel at the exact moment studios decide where to compete, so keep your dates current. Dates you enter
        yourself are authoritative: they always
        override anything our team has gathered.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">Can I link my registration portal?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        Yes! On your verified historical results pages, we can embed a prominent "Register for Next Year" button. This
        captures dancers and studio owners right when they are checking their results and are most engaged with your
        brand.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">What file formats are supported for upload?</div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        You can upload standard <span class="faq-highlight">.CSV</span>, <span class="faq-highlight">.TXT</span>, or
        <span class="faq-highlight">.XLSX
          (Excel)</span> files directly from your scoring system — but we also accept
        <span class="faq-highlight">PDFs and database exports</span>: SQL dumps (MySQL, PostgreSQL), SQLite or
        Access files, or a ZIP of any of these, up to 50&nbsp;MB per upload. Uploading years of history? No need to send
        events one by one — if sending everything at once is easier for you, zip your whole archive into a single
        upload, or email <span class="faq-highlight">hello@awardhome.com</span> with a Google Drive or Dropbox link, and
        our team takes it from there.
        Once uploaded, our team will parse the data, verify it, and integrate it into the dancer and
        studio portfolios.
        <br><br>
        Any layout works, but your results go live fastest when each row includes the
        <span class="faq-highlight">event name and date, routine name, placement, category or style, age division,
          dancer name(s), and studio</span>. Full dancer names (rather than initials) and consistent studio
        spellings help us match every award to the right dancer and studio — inconsistent
        entries can take careful hand-review, so cleaner files go live sooner. A ready-made CSV template is available on
        the
        <span class="faq-highlight">Upload Results</span> tab of your dashboard — a brand-new account opens straight
        onto it, with a three-step setup checklist (upload results, marketing profile, logo) guiding the rest.
      </div>
    </div>

